      "message": "**Issue #4 (🟢 Low Severity (NICE TO FIX))**: `${xpath_snmp_row_delete_button}` token substitution uses bare strings as sentinels\n\n**Issue**: `SNMP_IP` and `SNMP_PORT` are plain text sentinels embedded in the XPath string. If a real SNMP IP address ever begins with the literal substring `SNMP_IP` (unlikely but syntactically possible), or if the template variable is used without substitution, the XPath will silently match no element and produce a confusing `Element not found` error rather than an obvious template-expansion error.\n-\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n  # SNMP_IP and SNMP_PORT are token placeholders; use Replace String before passing to Selenium.\n  ${xpath_snmp_row_delete_button}   //tbody/tr[.//td[normalize-space(.)\u003d\u0027SNMP_IP\u0027] and .//td[normalize-space(.)\u003d\u0027SNMP_PORT\u0027]]//button[@title\u003d\u0027Delete destination\u0027]\n  ```\n\n**Why**: Documents the substitution contract for future maintainers and prevents accidental direct use of the variable without token replacement.",
