      "message": "**Issue #1 (🟡 Medium Severity (SHOULD FIX))**: `Verify SNMP Manager Configured On BMC` used for negative assertion — inverted logic risk\n\n**Issue**: `Verify SNMP Manager Configured On BMC` is designed as a positive assertion (it calls `List Should Contain Value` and fails if the manager is absent). Wrapping it with `Run Keyword And Return Status` to invert the result is functional, but if the underlying keyword changes its internal implementation (e.g. raises a different exception type or returns before the assertion), the `${status}` capture can silently return `${True}` for reasons unrelated to the manager being present. The established repo pattern for negative SNMP checks uses a dedicated keyword rather than inverting a positive one.\n-\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n      @{snmp_mgr_list}\u003d  Get SNMP Manager List\n      ${snmp_ip_port}\u003d  Catenate  ${snmp_ip}:${snmp_port}\n      List Should Not Contain Value  ${snmp_mgr_list}  snmp://${snmp_ip_port}\n      ...  msg\u003dSNMP manager was not deleted from BMC after GUI deletion.\n  ```\n\n**Why**: The current approach is fragile under keyword refactoring and masks the actual assertion logic. A direct `List Should Not Contain Value` call is unambiguous and aligns with the existing positive-check pattern.",
      "revId": "b0cb629d73d11351cfc203cd7d964a61ef98dea9",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
