      "message": "**Issue #3 (🟢 Low Severity (NICE TO FIX))**: `Read  delay\u003d5s` (flush) not strictly necessary before the first `Switch Connection`\n\n**Issue**: The flush occurs immediately after `Start SNMP Manager`, which backgrounds `snmptrapd` with `SSHLibrary.Write`. Any output buffered at this point would be startup noise from `snmptrapd` itself, not a prior trap. A `delay\u003d5s` flush here is safe but adds 5 s of wall-clock time without a documented race condition it is guarding against. The existing repo pattern does not flush before generating the error log.\n-\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n      SSHLibrary.Switch Connection  snmp_server\n      Read  delay\u003d1s    # Discard snmptrapd startup noise before triggering error log.\n  ```\n\n**Why**: Consistency with `delay\u003d1s` used in `Create Error Log On BMC And Verify Trap` and `Create Error On BMC And Verify Trap On Non Default Port`; reduces total test execution time by 4 s per run.",
